[numbers]
# Meitei number words as Meetei Mayek text writes them (AI4Bharat IndicCorp
# v2 Manipuri, CC0, whose number articles spell out 1-999; the units, tens,
# 100 and 1000 as listed in the Wikipedia article "Meitei language"): the
# units ꯑꯃꯥ ꯑꯅꯤ ꯑꯍꯨꯝ ꯃꯔꯤ ꯃꯉꯥ ꯇꯔꯨꯛ ꯇꯔꯦꯠ ꯅꯤꯄꯥꯟ ꯃꯥꯄꯟ, ꯇꯔꯥ 10, ꯀꯨꯟ 20, ꯀꯨꯟꯊ꯭ꯔꯥ
# 30, ꯅꯤꯐꯨ 40 ("two twenties"), ꯌꯥꯡꯈꯩ 50, ꯍꯨꯝꯐꯨ 60, ꯍꯨꯝꯐꯨꯇꯔꯥ 70, ꯃꯔꯤꯐꯨ 80,
# ꯃꯔꯤꯐꯨꯇꯔꯥ 90; a unit after a ten is one word with it, 1-3 in the forms
# ꯃꯊꯣꯏ ꯅꯤꯊꯣꯏ ꯍꯨꯝꯊꯣꯏ (ꯀꯨꯟꯃꯊꯣꯏ 21; 11 and 13 as Wikipedia lists them,
# ꯇꯔꯥꯃꯥꯊꯣꯏ ꯇꯔꯥꯍꯨꯝꯗꯣꯏ); the hundreds ꯆꯥ- with the unit (ꯆꯥꯝꯃꯥ 100, ꯆꯥꯅꯤ
# 200, ꯆꯥꯝꯉꯥ 500), followed by -ꯒ ꯁꯨꯞꯅ ("and, adding") when more follows
# (ꯆꯥꯅꯤꯒ ꯁꯨꯞꯅ ꯑꯃꯥ 201); above, the scale word comes first and its count
# after it (ꯂꯤꯁꯤꯡ ꯑꯅꯤ 2000, ꯂꯥꯈ ꯇꯔꯥ ten lakh, as the same text writes
# them), with the borrowed ꯂꯥꯈ and ꯀ꯭ꯔꯣꯔ for 10^5 and 10^7. Zero ꯐꯨꯟ
# (Wiktionary), point ꯄꯣꯏꯟꯇ and the rupee ꯂꯨꯄꯥ (said after the amount here;
# Meitei text often writes it before) as the same text uses them; minus and
# per cent are the English loans ꯃꯥꯏꯅꯁ and ꯄꯔꯁꯦꯟꯇ (no Meitei word found in
# the sources).
